1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,500
Supply chain finance fails when trust remains fragmented and off-chain.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,000
AttestFlow uses the Attestcoin protocol as its verifiable trust layer.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:16,500
This is not a single proof added after the workflow.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Attestcoin secures evidence, financing, ownership, and settlement end to end.

5
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:26,500
We begin by signing in as the supplier.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
The workspace shows each receivable and its lifecycle.

7
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,500
I click New Receivable.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
First, I upload the underlying supply contract and invoice.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,500
AttestFlow accepts PDF or text-based trade documents for analysis.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,000
I click AI Analyze and Autofill.

11
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:53,000
The AI extracts the buyer, supplier, contract number, and invoice number.

12
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:58,500
It also identifies the receivable amount and payment due date.

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The supplier reviews every extracted field before creating the record.

14
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:09,500
I click Create Receivable to submit the verified trade details.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The receivable hash now waits for confirmation from the buyer.

16
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Next, we switch to the core buyer.

17
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,000
The buyer reviews the contract, invoice, amount, and maturity date.

18
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:32,000
These details represent the real payment obligation.

19
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:37,000
I click Confirm Payable and connect the buyer wallet.

20
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:42,500
The wallet switches to the Creditcoin test network when required.

21
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The buyer signs a future EIP-three-zero-zero-nine payment authorization.

22
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:52,000
The server independently verifies and stores the signed authorization.

23
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:57,500
This confirms the payable without moving or locking buyer funds.

24
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,500
The authorization becomes executable only within its settlement window.

25
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The receivable status changes to Confirmed and Financeable.

26
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:12,000
The Attestcoin proof pipeline now enters its queued state.

27
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:17,500
It waits for a verifiable financing transaction as source evidence.

28
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Now we return to the supplier workspace.

29
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:29,500
The confirmed receivable is ready for non-recourse financing.

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,500
I click Start Financing Inquiry.

31
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
The wallet calls request Financing on the Attestcoin settlement contract.

32
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:44,000
The protocol stores the receivable hash, token, supplier, and face value.

33
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:49,000
Its Financing Requested event becomes the proof's source transaction.

34
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
We switch to the funder.

35
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:01,500
The funder reads the protocol request and opens the quote form.

36
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,500
I enter the financing percentage.

37
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:09,500
AttestFlow calculates the advance amount and annualized yield automatically.

38
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,500
I also set the offer expiration time.

39
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,000
The summary clearly shows the principal and total financing cost.

40
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:23,500
I confirm the quote through the Attestcoin protocol.

41
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:29,000
First, the funder approves the settlement contract to use mUSDC.

42
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:34,500
Then submit Offer records the terms and funder identity on-chain.

43
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:40,500
The same call locks the exact financing principal inside the contract.

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:45,500
Attestcoin exposes principal, yield, expiry, and acceptance status on-chain.

45
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
We switch back to the supplier.

46
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
The workspace displays the live, non-recourse financing offer.

47
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:01,500
I call accept Offer through the supplier wallet.

48
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The supplier confirms acceptance with the connected wallet.

49
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:11,000
Attestcoin atomically releases the locked principal to the supplier.

50
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:16,500
The accepted offer simultaneously identifies the funder as settlement recipient.

51
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,500
The receivable now shows Assigned and Funded.

52
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
There is no separate off-chain payment reconciliation step.

53
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:30,500
For this demonstration, the operator advances the receivable to maturity.

54
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:35,500
The bound payment authorization is now executable through Attestcoin.

55
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Finally, we return to the funder.

56
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:47,000
The settlement monitor shows the receivable is due.

57
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:50,000
I click Execute Relayer Settlement.

58
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:55,000
A restricted relayer calls settle With Authorization on Attestcoin.

59
00:04:55,500 --> 00:05:01,000
The protocol validates the payer, recipient, window, nonce, token, and amount.

60
00:05:01,500 --> 00:05:05,500
Anti-replay state prevents duplicate authorization or receivable settlement.

61
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,500
Attestcoin then credits a pull-payment balance to the funder.

62
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:16,000
The funder wallet calls claim against its own protocol balance.

63
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:21,500
No caller can redirect those settlement funds to another wallet.

64
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:26,500
The receivable is marked Paid and financing becomes Repaid.

65
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,500
Every protocol event and transaction hash remains independently verifiable.

66
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,500
Attestcoin also registers a composite audit evidence hash on-chain.

67
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:42,000
It binds receivable, authorization, source transaction, and source block hashes.

68
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:47,500
Two contracts and six protocol writes cover the complete lifecycle.

69
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:53,000
AttestFlow demonstrates deep Attestcoin usage, from evidence to final repayment.
